From: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 16:46:39 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: extend the manual RX calibration to the PON PCS

745 extends the manual RX calibration window to E2 silicon for the
Ethernet PCS (gdm4 / lan2). The PON PCS drives gdm2 -- on this board the
WAN port -- and has the same autocalibration weakness: the manual path
retries AIROHA_PCS_MAX_CALIBRATION_TRY times when FreqDet fails to lock,
the autocalibration path has no equivalent retry.

The PCS probe already reads AIROHA_SCU_PDIDR; just accept the PON PCS
compatible string there as well. The runtime effect is unchanged on E1/E2
silicon that 745 already covered for the Ethernet PCS, and it is what the
Ethernet PCS does today, so a board that boots today still boots.

Reported against the Gemtek W1700K (HW.2.0) as intermittent WAN failure;
the XR1710G wires gdm2 to the same pon_pcs (an7581.dtsi:959
pcs-handle = <&pon_pcs>).

Ported from the out-of-tree W1700K 6.18 patch set (Gilly1970).
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -1213,7 +1213,8 @@
 	 * manual rx calibration is needed. Extend the manual-calibration
 	 * threshold to include E2 silicon.
 	 */
-	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,an7581-pcs-eth")) {
+	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,an7581-pcs-eth") ||
+	    device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,an7581-pcs-pon")) {
 		u32 val;
 
 		ret = regmap_read(priv->scu, AIROHA_SCU_PDIDR, &val);
